  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA cold front will push through the area today, causing showers\nto taper off from west to east. Most of the region has received\nless than three quarters of an inch so far, with just a couple\nof higher spots in southeast Ohio. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA secondary cold front crosses Friday into Saturday leading to\nchances for more showers across the area, especially across\nsoutheast Ohio and northern West Virginia. \n\nMuch cooler air will move in behind the cold front for the \nweekend. As high pressure builds in later in the weekend and\ninto the next work week, nighttime temperatures are expected to\nget cold enough for frost and freezing temperatures.",
